1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,147
Asia runs on corner shops: 12 million kiranas in India, 1.

2
00:00:06,197 --> 00:00:10,000
3 million sari-sari stores, nearly 4 million warungs.

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:13,371
Almost none can get a bank loan.

4
00:00:14,321 --> 00:00:15,486
Meet Sunita Sharma.

5
00:00:15,536 --> 00:00:18,321
Eleven years running a kirana in Pune.

6
00:00:18,371 --> 00:00:21,966
Three weeks before Diwali, she needs ₹80,000 for stock.

7
00:00:22,016 --> 00:00:25,206
No credit score, so the bank says no,

8
00:00:25,256 --> 00:00:28,851
and she borrows at up to 5% a month.

9
00:00:29,701 --> 00:00:34,228
India's small businesses face a credit gap of ₹30 lakh crore.

10
00:00:34,278 --> 00:00:38,804
Over 9,000 NBFCs and nearly 1,500 co-operative banks want these customers.

11
00:00:38,854 --> 00:00:42,132
But checking one shop means a field visit,

12
00:00:42,182 --> 00:00:44,213
a ledger they can't read,

13
00:00:44,263 --> 00:00:47,125
and documents that are easy to forge.

14
00:00:49,075 --> 00:00:50,158
This is Kosha.

15
00:00:50,208 --> 00:00:53,181
It turns the records a shop already keeps

16
00:00:53,231 --> 00:00:56,203
into a credit passport any lender can trust.

17
00:00:57,853 --> 00:00:59,583
Sunita photographs her khata.

18
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:03,142
Gemini reads every handwritten Hindi line, translates it,

19
00:01:03,192 --> 00:01:06,701
and sorts it into sales, stock and credit.

20
00:01:07,351 --> 00:01:11,992
Then Kosha checks the evidence: supplier bills that match to the rupee,

21
00:01:12,042 --> 00:01:14,337
over ₹8,000 a day on UPI,

22
00:01:14,387 --> 00:01:16,682
and electricity bills paid on time.

23
00:01:17,332 --> 00:01:18,809
Gemini maps the neighbourhood,

24
00:01:18,859 --> 00:01:22,627
and five questions in Hindi are checked against her documents.

25
00:01:23,577 --> 00:01:27,819
Two minutes later: a score of 794, an ₹80,000 offer,

26
00:01:27,869 --> 00:01:29,965
and repayments that follow Diwali.

27
00:01:30,015 --> 00:01:34,687
Every reason links to its evidence, explained to her in Hindi.

28
00:01:35,527 --> 00:01:36,787
नमस्ते सुनीता जी।
Namaste, Sunita ji.

29
00:01:37,257 --> 00:01:39,587
आपके अच्छे रिकॉर्ड्स के आधार पर,
Based on your good records,

30
00:01:39,737 --> 00:01:43,207
आपकी दुकान अस्सी हज़ार रुपये तक के ऋण के लिए योग्य है।
your shop qualifies for a loan of up to ₹80,000.

31
00:01:44,617 --> 00:01:47,009
Sunita chooses which lenders see it,

32
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:51,079
and shares a QR code anyone can scan to verify.

33
00:01:51,129 --> 00:01:52,707
At her co-operative bank,

34
00:01:52,757 --> 00:01:55,964
Arjun checks the evidence and approves the loan.

35
00:01:57,308 --> 00:02:00,992
In Quezon City, a payment screenshot hides an extra ₱48,000.

36
00:02:01,042 --> 00:02:04,727
Gemini spots the different font, the balance doesn't add up,

37
00:02:04,777 --> 00:02:06,595
and the offer is held.

38
00:02:07,745 --> 00:02:09,529
And trust is built in.

39
00:02:09,579 --> 00:02:12,464
Sunita sees every lender who opens her passport.

40
00:02:12,514 --> 00:02:15,766
A new lender sees nothing until Kosha verifies them,

41
00:02:15,816 --> 00:02:18,700
and every action lands in an audit log.

42
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:22,369
Anyone who scans the QR sees only the public record,

43
00:02:22,419 --> 00:02:25,671
and its seal shows if a printout was changed.

44
00:02:26,821 --> 00:02:30,851
In numbers: 46 handwritten lines read in seconds.

45
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:33,911
4 of 4 supplier bills matched.

46
00:02:33,961 --> 00:02:36,461
12 cross-checks across 5 sources.

47
00:02:36,511 --> 00:02:40,032
About ten Gemini calls, a few cents,

48
00:02:40,082 --> 00:02:44,112
and under two minutes from photos to passport.

49
00:02:45,462 --> 00:02:47,421
And Sunita is one of millions.

50
00:02:47,471 --> 00:02:50,770
Rafiq, a tailor in Lucknow, earns most in wedding season,

51
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:54,453
so his repayments rise in winter and ease in the monsoon.

52
00:02:54,503 --> 00:02:57,802
Murugan sells 300 cups of chai a day in Chennai,

53
00:02:57,852 --> 00:03:01,485
all on UPI, and those small payments become a credit history.

54
00:03:01,535 --> 00:03:04,834
In Bandung, Ibu Sari keeps her warung's ledger in Bahasa,

55
00:03:04,884 --> 00:03:08,183
and a digital bank verifies her passport without a visit.

56
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:13,550
Any lender can use it: co-operative banks, NBFCs, digital banks, wholesalers.

57
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:17,520
Shops borrow at bank rates instead of 5% a month.

58
00:03:17,570 --> 00:03:19,902
Lenders review in minutes, not days.

59
00:03:19,952 --> 00:03:23,078
Free for shops; lenders pay per verified passport.

60
00:03:24,328 --> 00:03:26,941
Try it yourself, live, at kosha-ai.web.app.

61
00:03:26,991 --> 00:03:30,936
Pick a sample shop and watch Gemini read it,

62
00:03:30,986 --> 00:03:34,931
or sign in as a lender or an admin.

63
00:03:36,381 --> 00:03:39,797
Built on Gemini and Firebase, on Google Cloud.

64
00:03:39,847 --> 00:03:43,262
Every corner shop has a treasury of trust.

65
00:03:43,312 --> 00:03:45,861
Kosha lets the world see it.
